1
00:00:00,480 --> 00:00:02,700
This is ZeroKey Mate.

2
00:00:03,180 --> 00:00:05,800
It turns my iPhone into a companion.

3
00:00:06,160 --> 00:00:10,850
I can ask it for a beer, prove my age privately,

4
00:00:11,650 --> 00:00:13,500
and pay on Arc.

5
00:00:14,150 --> 00:00:18,400
The shop only needs to know that I am twenty or older.

6
00:00:18,770 --> 00:00:24,200
It does not need my name, address, or full date of birth.

7
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:26,150
Here is the real app.

8
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:30,050
These are edited takes from the physical device.

9
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:33,400
I ask Mate to buy a beer.

10
00:00:33,930 --> 00:00:38,320
I enter the card password privately, then tap my card.

11
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:41,700
The phone creates the age proof here.

12
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:52,700
After the store verifies it, I approve this exact payment.

13
00:00:55,970 --> 00:00:59,550
The purchase completes on Arc Testnet.

14
00:01:05,580 --> 00:01:08,320
I can open the receipt in the explorer.

15
00:01:09,930 --> 00:01:11,970
This uses test funds.

16
00:01:12,450 --> 00:01:13,930
No real beer is delivered.

17
00:01:14,740 --> 00:01:15,800
How does it work?

18
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:20,900
Speech recognition and the language model run on the iPhone.

19
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:27,200
Apple Foundation Models turns my request into a small, structured plan.

20
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,200
Mate checks the item, shop, and amount.

21
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:36,150
The model cannot access my card data or sign a payment.

22
00:01:36,730 --> 00:01:38,700
The proof is the key part.

23
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,450
Our Noir circuit checks the government signature,

24
00:01:42,910 --> 00:01:45,450
the card signature for this order,

25
00:01:45,850 --> 00:01:48,800
and that I am at least twenty.

26
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:51,950
It also checks the time limits.

27
00:01:52,670 --> 00:01:56,800
ProveKit, from World Foundation, runs the prover on the iPhone.

28
00:01:57,490 --> 00:02:02,750
The private card data becomes an age proof for this order.

29
00:02:03,150 --> 00:02:05,950
We use My Number card identity here.

30
00:02:06,050 --> 00:02:08,100
World ID is not connected.

31
00:02:08,620 --> 00:02:12,600
My birth date and card data stay on the phone.

32
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:17,250
The shop receives the proof and public order inputs.

33
00:02:18,050 --> 00:02:20,400
Payment addresses are still public.

34
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:24,450
The privacy boundary is specific and verifiable.

35
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:29,250
The store verifies the proof using our Age Gate contract on Arc.

36
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:34,400
Then Privy signs the exact payment I approve.

37
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:38,880
x402 carries that payment to the store,

38
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:40,880
which pays the network fee.

39
00:02:41,540 --> 00:02:45,350
We check the actual receipt before showing success.

40
00:02:46,260 --> 00:02:50,600
Age verification and the token transfer are separate steps.

41
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:53,150
Each layer has a clear job.

42
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:55,200
Apple powers the companion.

43
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:59,050
Noir and ProveKit handle the private proof.

44
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:03,080
Cloudflare runs the store and order recovery.

45
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:08,650
Privy, x402, and Arc complete the payment.

46
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:14,200
One physical-card run showed twelve seconds of local proof processing.

47
00:03:14,550 --> 00:03:17,650
We completed real test payments on Arc.

48
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:21,200
This is still an experimental testnet build.

49
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:23,400
Your companion. Your rules.

50
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:25,100
That is ZeroKey Mate.
